{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>For I will go to my land, etc.</b> One needs to know why it was necessary to say the word <b>I will go</b>, for is it not understood from his saying ״I will not go, but״ etc.? It may be explained by way of the words of the Sages of blessed memory (Mekhilta Yitro), and this is their language: ״And Moses sent his father-in-law״ — Rabbi Yehoshua says: he sent him away from the honor of the world. Rabbi Elazar haModa'i says: he said to him: Does a lamp give benefit except in a place of darkness? What do I benefit between the sun and the moon? Rather, I am going to my land and will convert all the people of my province and bring them to study, etc. Could it be that he went and did not do so? Behold it says (Judges 1:16) ״And the children of the Kenite״ etc. From within their words it implies that Rabbi Yehoshua holds that Yitro did not convert, and Moses sent him away from the honor of the world; whereas according to Rabbi Elazar he did convert. And according to the words of both of them, the addition of <b>I will go</b> is explained correctly. According to Rabbi Yehoshua, the intention is to say in this manner: <b>I will not go, but to my land</b> — and not for the reason of fondness for my land alone, for aside from that I would have stayed; that is not so, but rather <b>I will go</b> in any case. And according to the reasoning of Rabbi Elazar, in this manner: <b>I will not go</b> — meaning, in firm commitment to this going; <b>but to my land and to my kindred</b> — meaning, to that which is fitting for the people of my land and my kindred, <b>I will go</b> to convert them and bring them back. And he doubled to say ״my land and my kindred״ to say: if I find a place, I will convert all the people of my province, and at least the people of my kindred."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:25.848031769Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}